// Title: NtdllPipe Like Activity Execution
// Sigma ID: bbc865e4-7fcd-45a6-8ff1-95ced28ec5b2
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-03-05 | Modified: 2023-03-07
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment
// Description: Detects command that type the content of ntdll.dll to a different file or a pipe in order to
//   evade AV / EDR detection. As seen being used in the POC NtdllPipe
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20220306121156/https://www.x86matthew.com/view_post?id=ntdll_pipe
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmd_ntdllpipe_redirect.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "type %windir%\\system32\\ntdll.dll" or ProcessCommandLine contains "type %systemroot%\\system32\\ntdll.dll" or ProcessCommandLine contains "type c:\\windows\\system32\\ntdll.dll" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\ntdll.dll > \\\\.\\pipe\\"
